Ukraine’s Main Intelligence Directorate (GUR) “Prymary” Special Unit carried out precision strikes on several high-value Russian assets, including:
• A railway bridge over the North Crimean Canal;
• 9 communications, electronic warfare (EW), electronic intelligence (ELINT), radar, and MESH relay towers;
A Su-30SM multirole fighter (failed);
• A 55Zh6U Nebo-U radar;
• A command post of a P-18 Terek radar;
• Two Kasta-2E radars;
• An L-39 Albatros jet trainer/light attack aircraft;
• A BK-10 high-speed assault boat;
• A BK-16 high-speed transport and landing boat;
• A Mangust high-speed patrol boat.
